 35CL c  1996Il02,1997Il03: A 500-MeV proton beam was produced from the TRIUMF  
 35CL2c  cyclotron and bombarded a CaO powder target. The spallation reaction   
 35CL3c  products diffused out of the target and were selectively ionized at a  
 35CL4c  Re surface. A=36 singly charged ions were selected by a magnetic mass  
 35CL5c  analyzer and implanted into a carbon foil at 7.0|*10{+5} pps. Protons  
 35CL6c  and |a particles were detected using a 30-|mm silicon surface barrier  
 35CL7c  detector with FWHM=23 keV. {+32}S and {+35}Cl recoils were detected    
 35CL8c  using an MCP in a back-to-back geometry for timing stop signals.       
 35CL9c  Measured E{-p}(>0.5 MeV) and I{-p} for 15 proton peaks, E{-|a}(>1.5    
 35CLAc  MeV) and I{-|a} for 19 |a peaks, p(recoil)-coin, and |a(recoil)-coin.  
 35CLBc  Deduced levels, J, |p, decay branching ratios, log {Ift}, partial decay
 35CLCc  widths for {+36}Ar, and ratios of {+35}Cl(p,|a){+32}S to               
 35CLDc  {+35}Cl(p,|g){+36}Ar reaction rates.                                   
 35CL d
 35CL c  1980Es01: A 20-MeV proton beam was produced from the University of     
 35CL2c  Jyvaskyla MC-20 cyclotron and bombarded {+36}Ar-deposited Al foils. The
 35CL3c  {+36}Ar(p,n) reaction products were thermalized by helium, transported 
 35CL4c  with NaCl-loaded helium into a measurement chamber, and deposited onto 
 35CL5c  a fast-transport Al-coated mylar tape. Protons and |a particles were   
 35CL6c  detected using 14- and 26-|mm fully depleted (FWHM=40 keV) and 100-|mm 
 35CL7c  partially depleted Si(Au) surface barrier detectors. A polyethene      
 35CL8c  absorber foil was placed in front of Si(Au) to cause an energy shift   
 35CL9c  for distinguishing p/|a. Measured E{-p}(>0.5 MeV) and I{-p} for 11     
 35CLAc  proton peaks, E{-|a}(>2.0 MeV) and I{-|a} for 12 |a peaks. Deduced     
 35CLBc  levels, J, |p, decay branching ratios, log {Ift}, and partial decay    
 35CLCc  widths for {+36}Ar.                                                    
 35CL d
 35CL c  1980Ew01: A 600-MeV proton beam was produced from the synchrocyclotron 
 35CL2c  at CERN-ISOLDE and bombarded a ScC{-2} target. The {+45}Sc(p,7n3p)     
 35CL3c  spallation reaction products diffused out of the target and reached a  
 35CL4c  tungsten surface ionization source where potassium isotopes were       
 35CL5c  selectively ionized. The beam was extracted from the ion source,       
 35CL6c  separated by the ISOLDE analyzing magnet, and collected by a carbon    
 35CL7c  foil for proton measurements. Protons and |a particles were detected   
 35CL8c  using 20-|mm and 100-|mm silicon surface barrier detectors with FWHM=35
 35CL9c  and 23 keV. Measured E{-p}(>0.5 MeV) and I{-p} for 3 proton peaks,     
 35CLAc  E{-|a} and I{-|a} for 4 |a peaks. Deduced levels, J, |p, and decay     
 35CLBc  branching ratios for {+36}Ar.                                          
 35CL d  
